From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gpl: timing-driven pin pull (-timing_driven_pin_pull)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A net's timing weight scales the whole net. A failing sink of a
broadcast net that sits inside the net's bounding box feels no HPWL
force and an exponentially small weighted-average force, so the path
through it is never pulled straight; the timing-blind initial placement
sets the order and Nesterov keeps it.

-timing_driven_pin_pull (off by default, needs -timing_driven) adds a
two-pin attraction between each failing sink and its driver:

- Slacks are read inside Resizer::findResizeSlacks, on the netlist the
  virtual repair_design buffered, through a new optional callback
  between findResizeSlacks1() and the journal restore. Top-level output
  ports are read through the net's terms. The input of a buffer or
  inverter that rebuffering removed takes the worst slack of its loads.
- A failing connection's weight is strength (16) times the heavier of
  its two cells' other nets; it doubles (growth 1) at every update it
  still fails and is kept once it meets timing.
- Initial placement runs again after a timing analysis of its result
  (2 rounds by default), each pull a B2B spring of a two-pin net. In
  Nesterov each pull is the closed-form weighted-average length of the
  two-pin net {driver, sink} in the wirelength force and preconditioner.
  Pulls are not nets: HPWL is unchanged.

Options -timing_driven_pin_pull_strength, _growth, _max and
_initial_rounds; messages GPL-196 to 199; validator IDs 432 to 435.
With the flag off there is no PinPull object and every new line sits
behind an empty-list check.

Tests: pin_pull_test (the path_shape designs of the carried 0219 suite,
pulls given through a placePulled hook: broadcast path straightens,
swapped clusters straighten, 8 threads equal 1, the closed form matches
the two-pin net's WA gradient).

Not upstreamed. Applies after the carried OpenROAD patches and
0219-openroad-gpl-placement-regression-tests.patch. Retires with a
//:bump onto an OpenROAD that carries this or an equivalent pull
(check_carried_patches says ABSORBED). Held until XiangShan reaches
2,000 ps at global route in bazel-orfs, or that campaign ends; then a
new topic upstream, with 0219.

